            <ArticleTitle>Peritoneal tuberculosis due to Mycobacterium caprae.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>50-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.idcr.2016.02.010</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The incidence of tuberculosis in humans due to Mycobacterium caprae is very low and is almost confined to Europe. We report a case of a previously healthy 41-year-old Moroccan with a 6 month history of abdominal pain, weight loss, fatigue and diarrhea. A diagnosis of peritoneal tuberculosis due to M. caprae was made.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
